t in their transcript.\");\n    line(\"Fix the corpus before scoring. The quotes are the ground truth; a quote that does not match is\");\n    line(\"a ground truth that does not exist, and every recall number computed against it is wrong.\");\n    process.exitCode = 1;\n    throw new Error(\"unresolved corpus labels\");\n  }\n\n  /* The local engine, always. The whole benchmark runs keyless by design: a number that requires an API\n   * key to reproduce is not a number a judge can check, and ┬º7.5 lists keyless verification as a demo\n   * requirement for the same reason. */\n  return { corpus: load.corpus, load, engine: createLocalEngine(), engineId: localEngineId() };\n}\n\nexport function banner(text: string): void {\n  const rule = \"=\".repeat(Math.max(text.length, 78));\n  process.stdout.write(\"\\n\" + rule + \"\\n\" + text + \"\\n\" + rule + \"\\n\");\n}\n\nexport function heading(text: string): void {\n  process.stdout.write(\"\\n--- \" + text + \" \" + \"-\".repeat(Math.max(0, 72 - text.length)) + \"\\n\");\n}\n\nexport function line(text: string): void {\n  process.stdout.write(text + \"\\n\");\n}\n\nexport function blank(): void {\n  process.stdout.write(\"\\n\");\n}\n\nexport function write(filePath: string, contents: string): void {\n  const absolute = resolvePath(process.cwd(), filePath);\n  mkdirSync(dirname(absolute), { recursive: true });\n  writeFileSync(absolute, contents, \"utf8\");\n  line(\"wrote \" + filePath + \" (\" + contents.length.toLocaleString(\"en-US\") + \" bytes)\");\n}\n\n/** A `--flag value` reader. Unknown flags are reported rather than ignored, because a typo'd flag that\n *  silently falls back to a default produces a run the operator believes was configured differently. */\nexport function readArgs(argv: readonly string[]): Map<string, string> {\n  const out = new Map<string, string>();\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < argv.length; i += 1) {\n    const token = argv[i];\n    if (token === undefined || !token.startsWith(\"--\")) continue;\n\n    const key = token.slice(2);\n    const next = argv[i + 1];\n    if (next !== undefined && !next.startsWith(\"--\")) {\n      out.set(key, next);\n      i += 1;\n    } else {\n      out.set(key, \"true\");\n    }\n  }\n\n  const known = new Set([\"out\", \"json\", \"engine\", \"only\", \"quick\"]);\n  for (const key of out.keys()) {\n    if (!known.has(key)) line(\"note: unknown flag --\" + key + \" ignored (known: \" + [...known].join(\", \") + \")\");\n  }\n\n  return out;\n}\n"},"tags":["fixable"],"source":null},{"category":"lint/style/useTemplate","severity":"error","description":"Template literals are preferred over string concatenation.","message":[{"elements":["Emphasis"],"content":"Template"},{"elements":[],"content":" literals are preferred over "},{"elements":["Emphasis"],"content":"string concatenation."}],"advices":{"advices":[{"log":["info",[{"elements":[],"content":"Unsafe fix: Use a "},{"elements":["Emphasis"],"content":"template literal"},{"elements":[],"content":"."}]]},{"diff":{"dictionary":"/**\n * `npm run demo:verify` ΓÇö build the seed, verify every beat, run the dry runs.\n *  heading(\"Seed\");\n  const seed = await buildSeed();\n  line(\n    \"`built in \" +${(seed.durationMs / 1000).toFixed(1) + \"}s ┬╖seed.decisions\" decisions ┬╖+\n    seed.premises premises ┬╖ engine \" + seed.engineId.kind}`,\n  );\n  for (const warning of seed.warnings) line(\"  warning: \" + warning);  process.exitCode = 1;\n});\n","ops":[{"diffOp":{"equal":{"range":[0,88]}}},{"equalLines":{"line_count":32}},{"diffOp":{"equal":{"range":[88,148]}}},{"diffOp":{"equal":{"range":[148,153]}}},{"diffOp":{"delete":{"range":[153,154]}}},{"diffOp":{"insert":{"range":[154,155]}}},{"diffOp":{"equal":{"range":[155,163]}}},{"diffOp":{"delete":{"range":[163,167]}}},{"diffOp":{"equal":{"range":[88,89]}}},{"diffOp":{"insert":{"range":[167,169]}}},{"diffOp":{"equal":{"range":[169,204]}}},{"diffOp":{"delete":{"range":[204,208]}}},{"diffOp":{"insert":{"range":[208,209]}}},{"diffOp":{"equal":{"range":[209,213]}}},{"diffOp":{"delete":{"range":[163,167]}}},{"diffOp":{"equal":{"range":[204,205]}}},{"diffOp":{"insert":{"range":[167,169]}}},{"diffOp":{"equal":{"range":[213,227]}}},{"diffOp":{"delete":{"range":[204,206]}}},{"diffOp":{"insert":{"range":[208,209]}}},{"diffOp":{"equal":{"range":[204,205]}}},{"diffOp":{"delete":{"range":[227,229]}}},{"diffOp":{"equal":{"range":[229,241]}}},{"diffOp":{"delete":{"range":[163,165]}}},{"diffOp":{"equal":{"range":[204,205]}}},{"diffOp":{"delete":{"range":[241,247]}}},{"diffOp":{"insert":{"range":[167,169]}}},{"diffOp":{"equal":{"range":[247,260]}}},{"diffOp":{"delete":{"range":[204,208]}}},{"diffOp":{"insert":{"range":[208,209]}}},{"diffOp":{"equal":{"range":[260,280]}}},{"diffOp":{"delete":{"range":[280,284]}}},{"diffOp":{"insert":{"range":[167,169]}}},{"diffOp":{"equal":{"range":[284,302]}}},{"diffOp":{"insert":{"range":[302,304]}}},{"diffOp":{"equal":{"range":[304,380]}}},{"equalLines":{"line_count":33}},{"diffOp":{"equal":{"range":[380,408]}}}]}}]},"verboseAdvices":{"advices":[]},"location":{"path":{"file":".\\src\\eval\\demo\\cli.ts"},"span":[1469,1630],"sourceCode":"/**\n * `npm run demo:verify` ΓÇö build the seed, verify every beat, run the dry runs.\n *\n * Phase 7 ┬╖ sub-phase 7.5\n *\n * The rehearsal command. It answers three questions in order, and stops at the first one that fails:\n *   1. does the seed build at all\n *   2. does every beat of the script have something to show\n *   3. does it do the same thing three times in a row\n *\n * Keyless throughout. If this command needs an API key to pass, the demo is not verifiable and the\n * requirement in ┬º7.5 has not been met.\n */\n\nimport { banner, blank, heading, line, readArgs, write } from \"../cli\";\nimport { buildSeed, describeReset, resetDemo } from \"./kit\";\nimport { renderScript } from \"./script\";\nimport { renderVerification, verifyDemo } from \"./verify\";\nimport { REQUIRED_DRY_RUNS, renderDryRuns, runDryRuns } from \"./